```java
public WaveView claim(long releaseId, ClaimWaveRequest request) {
    String fingerprint = String.join("|", "wave.claim", request.operator(), String.valueOf(releaseId));
    return idempotency.execute(request.requestId(), "wave.claim", fingerprint, () -> {
        ReleaseOrder order = releaseRepository.findByIdForUpdate(releaseId)
                .orElseThrow(() -> ApiException.notFound("RELEASE_NOT_FOUND", ...));
        if (order.releaseType() != ReleaseType.TOPOLOGY) throw badRequest("NOT_TOPOLOGY_RELEASE", ...);
        if (order.status() != ReleaseStatus.ACTIVE) throw conflict("RELEASE_NOT_ACTIVE", ...);
        List<String> nodes = topologyRepository.findNodes(releaseId);
        List<TopologyEdge> edges = topologyRepository.findEdges(releaseId);
        Map<String, Device> devices = deviceRepository.findByIds(nodes) → map;
        Set<String> claimed = new HashSet<>(taskRepository.findDeviceIdsByRelease(releaseId));
        // adjacency
        Map<String, Set<String>> adj = ...;
        // eligible
        List<String> eligible = nodes.stream().filter(id -> {
            Device d = devices.get(id);
            if (claimed.contains(id) || d.down()) return false;
            if (!d.currentVersion().equals(order.fromVersion()) || d.bucketNo() >= order.ratio()) return false;
            // neighbors must be healthy (not down) and without active installation
            for (String n : adj.get(id)) {
                Device nd = devices.get(n);
                if (nd.down()) return false;
            }
            return true;
        }).sorted().toList();
        List<String> selected = selectMaxIndependent(eligible, adj);
        if (selected.isEmpty()) throw unprocessable("NO_WAVE_CANDIDATE", "当前无可领取的设备集合");
        int waveSeq = waveRepository.nextWaveSeq(releaseId);
        long waveId = waveRepository.insert(releaseId, waveSeq, selected.size());
        List<WaveMemberView> members = new ArrayList<>();
        for (String deviceId : selected) {
            waveRepository.insertMember(waveId, deviceId);
            long taskId = taskRepository.insert(releaseId, deviceId);
            deviceRepository.updateDown(deviceId, true);
            members.add(new WaveMemberView(deviceId, taskId));
        }
        return new WaveView(waveId, releaseId, waveSeq, members);
    }, WaveView.class);
}
```

Wait — "受已有活跃安装邻居阻断": neighbor with active installation. A neighbor with PENDING task is down (wave-created) — covered by down check. But also neighbor could have a PENDING task created... only via waves for topology releases. Covered. But what about the neighbor's *own* claimed-but-cancelled? Cancelled releases down. OK.

Also should the device itself with PENDING task be excluded — claimed set covers all tasks.

selectMaxIndependent: enumerate subsets of eligible (≤10 → 2^10). For each subset, check independent (no edge within), track best by (size desc, lexicographic asc), cap size at 5.

```java
private List<String> selectMaxIndependent(List<String> eligible, Map<String, Set<String>> adj) {
    int n = eligible.size();
    List<String> best = List.of();
    for (int mask = 1; mask < (1 << n); mask++) {
        if (Integer.bitCount(mask) > MAX_WAVE_SIZE) continue;
        if (Integer.bitCount(mask) < best.size()) continue; // can't beat... actually need <= check
        List<String> subset = ...;
        if (!isIndependent(subset, adj)) continue;
        if (subset.size() > best.size() || (subset.size() == best.size() && compareLex(subset, best) < 0)) best = subset;
    }
    return best;
}
```

Note eligible sorted, so subsets generated in sorted order. Lexicographic comparison of lists.

Edge case: eligible up to 10 → 1024 iterations, fine. If eligible could be > 20, mask overflow — but graph ≤ 10 nodes so eligible ≤ 10. Good.

